Fixes #27809

When a prop decides whether a call inside `try` throws, the value the `catch` assigns was treated as a constant, so anything built from it was cached once per mount.

```jsx
function Component({ value }) {
  let status = "valid";
  try {
    validate(value); // throws when `value` is falsy
  } catch {
    status = "invalid";
  }
  return <div>{status}</div>;
}
```

```diff
-  if ($[0] === Symbol.for("react.memo_cache_sentinel")) {
+  if ($[0] !== status) {
     t1 = <div>{status}</div>;
```

Before this PR, changing `value` from `1` to `0` still rendered `valid`.

## Cause

`infer_reactive_places` makes a value reactive when a reactive branch decides which assignment reaches it, but it only counts `if`, ternaries and `switch` as branches. A call that may throw inside `try` also decides which assignment runs, the one after it or the one in `catch`, and it was ignored.

Babel's React Compiler has the same limitation in [`isControlledBlock`](compiler/packages/babel-plugin-react-compiler/src/Inference/ControlDominators.ts#L26-L56). babel-plugin-react-compiler 1.0.0 and upstream main (built from source at `ab0d927f`) give the same stale output for both new fixtures.

## Fix

Treat a block that may throw to a `catch` as a branch. It counts as reactive when it reads a reactive value, like `validate(value)`, or when whether it runs is decided by a reactive branch, like `if (strict) { fail(); }`, or by an earlier such block.

