Rest parameters are stored separately from ordinary parameters, so the empty-IIFE check could discard calls whose rest destructuring runs default initializers. Check all parameters before removing the call, and reject destructured rest bindings when recording pure-function summaries.

```js
var n = 0;
(function (...[v = n++]) {})();
console.log(n);
```

This now prints `1` after minification instead of `0`. Regression tests cover function and arrow forms, object rest patterns, and destructuring that throws.

